<LanguageData>

  <!-- Weapon labels follow Odyssey's own French uniques ("arc long unique", "fusil d'assaut unique"):
       the adjective postposes, and "unique" is invariant in gender, so the same form serves the
       feminine weapons (hache, épée longue, masse, lance) and the masculine ones (glaive, couteau,
       marteau de guerre) alike.

       namerLabels are bare lowercase nouns with no gender marker, matching Odyssey's French namer,
       which never places an agreeing adjective or article beside [weapon_type] precisely because its
       gender is unknowable there. -->

